BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:dd8cd7300f00e6e717fba574@greenville-kid-calendar
DTSTAMP:20260925T151443Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T203000
SUMMARY:Neighborhood Night
LOCATION:Upcountry History Museum\, 540 Buncombe Street\, Greenville\, SC\,
  29601
DESCRIPTION:Access for All! UHM is open on the first Thursday evening of se
 lect months throughout 2026. The Museum operates with the firm belief that
  its exhibits\, events\, and programming should be accessible to all\, reg
 ardless of cultural\, ethnic\, geographic\, or socioeconomic differences. 
 The Neighborhood Night initiative\, introduced in 2015\, provides free acc
 ess to educational programming for underserved children\, families\, and a
 dults. WHEN: Thursday\, October 1st | 5:30 p.m. – 8:30 p.m. WHERE: Upcou
 ntry History Museum HOW: Drop in to explore the Museum and its changing ex
 hibitions. No registration is required. WHY: Neighborhood Nights demonstra
 te the Museum’s commitment to accessibility\, regardless of economic con
 straints by providing full access to the Museum’s diverse exhibitions. C
 OST: FREE! QUES Source: Upcountry History Museum. Check the linked organiz
 er page before leaving.
URL:https://upcountryhistory.org/event/neighborhood-night-37/
END:VEVENT
